# Day 10 - SQL Aggregate Functions & COUNT()

Today I practiced SQL aggregate functions, GROUP BY, and different behaviors of the COUNT() function with NULL values.

## Topics Covered

- Aggregate Functions
- MAX()
- MIN()
- AVG()
- ROUND()
- SUM()
- COUNT()
- COUNT(*)
- COUNT(1)
- COUNT(column)
- COUNT(DISTINCT column)
- COUNT(NULL)
- NULL comparison
- GROUP BY
- ORDER BY
- Understanding NULL values
- Aggregate vs Non-Aggregate Columns

## Aggregate Functions

Aggregate functions perform calculations on multiple rows and return a single result.

Examples:

```sql
SELECT 
    MAX(sal),
    MIN(sal),
    ROUND(AVG(sal), 2),
    COUNT(*),
    SUM(sal)
FROM emp;
